These made-up lists show a small numerical gap. They are not real embeddings of these words.

```javascript
const hot = [1, 2];
const cold = [1, 3];
const distance = Math.hypot(
  hot[0] - cold[0], hot[1] - cold[1]
);
console.log(distance);
```

It prints 1. The positions 0 and 1 pick the first and second numbers. Math.hypot combines the differences into a straight-line distance.
